{
  "info": {
    "name": "Chat — Customer portal (owner or teammate)",
    "description": "The customer’s side of chat: ten endpoints. There is no contact list, because there is nobody to choose between — a customer’s counterpart is the company’s assigned accounting manager, and the server resolves it from companyId alone.\n\nThe owner and a teammate behave identically, and each gets their OWN thread: a teammate cannot read the owner’s conversation.\n\nHOW TO USE\n1. Set `baseUrl` (http://localhost:3000/api locally, https://portal-backend-dev.vercel.app/api for dev), `email`, `password` and `companyId` in the collection variables.\n2. Run \"0. Sign in\" -> \"1. Password\", read the emailed 6-digit code, put it in the `otp` variable, run \"2. Verify code\". The token saves itself.\n3. Run the rest top to bottom. conversationId, messageId, uploadKey and attachmentId all save themselves as you go, so nothing needs copy-pasting.\n\nEvery endpoint takes companyId, and none of them will answer without it: a chat list merged across companies would put two clients on one screen.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Sign in",
      "description": "Two steps, because this API sends a one-time code by email. Run \"Password\", read the 6-digit code out of the user's mailbox, put it in the `otp` variable, then run 'Verify code'. The access token is saved automatically — every other request here already carries it.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Password",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
            "description": "Answers 202, not 200: the password was right but you are not signed in yet. The challengeId is saved for the next request.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.challengeId) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('challengeId', body.data.challengeId);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('challenge issued', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(202));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Verify code",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/otp",
            "description": "Put the emailed 6-digit code in the `otp` collection variable first. Saves the access token.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"action\": \"verify\",\n  \"challengeId\": \"{{challengeId}}\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.accessToken) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', body.data.accessToken);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('signed in', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Threads",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Open (or reuse) a conversation",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/conversations",
            "description": "No participantUserId: your counterpart is this company’s accounting manager, read from companies.accounting_manager_user_id. Idempotent, so it answers 200 whether or not the thread already existed. A company with no manager staffed answers 409.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"companyId\": \"{{companyId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.id) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('conversationId', body.data.id);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('conversation ready', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "My conversations on this company",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/conversations?companyId={{companyId}}",
            "description": "Only the threads you are one of the two sides of. Never anybody else’s."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Messages in a thread",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages?limit=50",
            "description": "Newest first. Add &before={{cursor}} to scroll further back, or &after=<cursor> to catch up after a dropped live connection. Each message carries its sender, its derived receiver, and both email addresses — none of which are stored columns."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.nextCursor) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('cursor', body.data.nextCursor);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Send a message",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages",
            "description": "Saves the new message id, so \"Mark as read\" and \"Delete a message\" below already know it.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"body\": \"Hello from Postman.\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.id) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('messageId', body.data.id);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('sent', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Mark as read",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/conversations/{{conversationId}}/read",
            "description": "Stamps only what the OTHER side sent — you cannot mark your own message read. Answers with the badge’s new value. Send an empty body {} to mark the whole thread.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"upToMessageId\": \"{{messageId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Unread badge",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/unread-count?companyId={{companyId}}",
            "description": "Everything unread across every thread you are in on this company."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete a message",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/messages/{{messageId}}",
            "description": "Soft delete, and only your own. Being in a thread does not make the other person’s words yours to remove."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Attachments",
      "description": "Three steps, because the bytes must not travel through the API — it runs on a host that refuses a request body past about 4.5 MB. Ask for a signed URL, PUT the file straight to Supabase, then send a message naming the key you were given.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Ask for an upload URL",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/attachments/upload-url",
            "description": "The key is scoped to THIS conversation (chat/<conversationId>/<random>.pdf), which is what stops a file uploaded for one client’s thread being attached to another’s. Accepted types: PDF, Word, Excel, CSV, plain text, images.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"conversationId\": \"{{conversationId}}\",\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"fileName\": \"statement.pdf\",\n      \"mimeType\": \"application/pdf\",\n      \"sizeBytes\": 12345\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const upload = body.data && body.data.uploads && body.data.uploads[0];",
                  "if (upload) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('uploadUrl', upload.uploadUrl);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('uploadKey', upload.key);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('ticket issued', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. PUT the file to Supabase",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/pdf"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{uploadUrl}}",
            "body": {
              "mode": "file",
              "file": {
                "src": null
              }
            },
            "description": "Goes to Supabase, NOT to this API — no Authorization header, the signature is in the URL. Open the Body tab and pick a real PDF from your machine before sending. A successful PUT answers 200 with the stored path."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Send the message with the file",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages",
            "description": "The size and type recorded are read back from the bucket, never taken from this request. Leave \"body\" out entirely to send a file with no caption.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"body\": \"Statement attached.\",\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"{{uploadKey}}\",\n      \"fileName\": \"statement.pdf\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const attachment = body.data && body.data.attachments && body.data.attachments[0];",
                  "if (attachment) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('attachmentId', attachment.id);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('sent with attachment', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Get a download link",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/attachments/{{attachmentId}}/download-url",
            "description": "A signed link that expires in about a minute, checked against the thread first. Works for downloads and for inline image previews. The storage key itself is never returned."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Live",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Realtime token (live updates)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/realtime-token",
            "description": "The credential the browser opens its Supabase Realtime connection with — read-only, ~30 minutes. Needs SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET in .env; without it this answers 503 and chat still works over REST, just without live updates. Run db/schema/21_add_chat_realtime.sql first."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.token) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('realtimeToken', body.data.token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
